From: OpenStick Builder <noreply@openstick.local>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wcn36xx: allow slow firmware TX acknowledgements

Some UFI001C firmware revisions return OTA TX completion indications later
than the 100 ms watchdog used by wcn36xx. The watchdog clears tx_ack_skb
first, so the valid but late completion is reported as a spurious indication.
Authentication management frames then reach mac80211 as unacknowledged and
connection setup can time out.

Keep the firmware's single-outstanding-ACK design, but allow one second for
the indication. Log watchdog expirations so field tests can distinguish this
case from lost DXE completions. This intentionally avoids changing descriptor
ownership or queue ordering.

NOTE (2026-09-09): this patch predates the actual UFI001C Wi-Fi diagnosis and
does not fix it. Association failed because pm8916 l9 (vddpa) was never
enabled, so the transmit power amplifier was unpowered and no AP could ever
acknowledge a frame -- no watchdog value can wait out an ACK that will not be
sent. scripts/build_kernel.sh now marks that rail regulator-always-on in the
board's device tree, which is the fix. The change below is retained purely as
a diagnostic: with the rail powered the watchdog should never expire, so the
message firing again means the PA is unpowered on that unit.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/dxe.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/dxe.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/dxe.c
index 9013f05..7f4ccf7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/dxe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/dxe.c
@@ -27,6 +27,9 @@
 #include "wcn36xx.h"
 #include "txrx.h"
 
+/* Older WCNSS firmware can take longer than 100 ms to report an OTA ACK. */
+#define WCN36XX_TX_ACK_TIMEOUT msecs_to_jiffies(1000)
+
 static void wcn36xx_ccu_write_register(struct wcn36xx *wcn, int addr, int data)
 {
 	wcn36xx_dbg(WCN36XX_DBG_DXE,
@@ -379,6 +382,7 @@ static void wcn36xx_dxe_tx_timer(struct timer_list *t)
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
 
 	/* TX Timeout */
+	wcn36xx_warn("TX ACK indication timed out after 1000 ms\n");
 	wcn36xx_dbg(WCN36XX_DBG_DXE, "TX timeout\n");
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&wcn->dxe_lock, flags);
@@ -429,6 +433,7 @@ static void reap_tx_dxes(struct wcn36xx *wcn, struct wcn36xx_dxe_ch *ch)
 						ieee80211_free_txskb(wcn->hw, wcn->tx_ack_skb);
 					wcn->tx_ack_skb = ctl->skb; /* Tracking ref */
-					mod_timer(&wcn->tx_ack_timer, jiffies + HZ / 10);
+					mod_timer(&wcn->tx_ack_timer,
+						  jiffies + WCN36XX_TX_ACK_TIMEOUT);
 					spin_unlock(&wcn->dxe_lock);
 				}
 				/* do not free, ownership transferred to mac80211 status cb */
-- 
